  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following statements are correct about zeolite?<br />\r<math><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Zeolites are aluminosilicates having three dimensional network<br />\r<math><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Shape selectivity of zeolites depends upon porous structures of the catalyst<br />\r<math><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Zeolites are synthetic microporous aluminosilicates which do not exist naturally<br />\r<math><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Zeolites are open structures of silica in which trivalent aluminium substitute by a fraction of silicon atoms",
